  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): When a SOC 1 Type II report contains a qualified opinion, the user entity''s auditor should evaluate the nature and significance of the exceptions and assess their potential impact on the user entity''s financial statement assertions. Per AT-C Section 320, additional procedures such as testing compensating controls or expanding substantive testing may be needed.
Wrong (A): Disregarding the report entirely is inappropriate because a qualified opinion does not make the SOC 1 report unreliable — it still provides useful information about the service organization''s controls.
