-- Q3893: SOC Reporting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): A bridge letter is a written management representation from the service organization addressing whether significant changes occurred to the system, controls, or control environment between the SOC report end date and a specified later date. Per AICPA SOC reporting guidance, it helps the user auditor evaluate the gap period but provides only management representations, not independent auditor assurance.
Wrong (B): A bridge letter does not convert a Type I report into a Type II report — these are separate engagement types requiring distinct examination procedures.
Wrong (C): A bridge letter is not a communication mechanism between auditors; it is a management representation from the service organization.
Wrong (D): A bridge letter does not extend the formal assurance coverage of the existing report — it only provides management''s representations about the intervening period.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3893;

-- Q3894: SOC Reporting [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AT-C Section 205, the description of tests and results section in a SOC 2 Type II report presents each control tested, the specific testing procedures performed (inquiry, inspection, observation, reperformance), the nature of each exception identified, and management''s response or corrective action. This transparency allows user auditors to evaluate whether exceptions are isolated or systemic.
Wrong (A): Exceptions are not disclosed separately in a confidential appendix — AT-C 205 requires exceptions to be disclosed within the report alongside the related control tests.
Wrong (B): The report does not include the service organization''s revenue or profitability, as these are irrelevant to control effectiveness testing.
Wrong (D): The user entity''s own internal control assessment is not part of the service organization''s SOC 2 report — each entity maintains its own documentation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3894;

-- Q3898: SOC Reporting [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AT-C Section 320.31-33, the system description provides comprehensive information about the service organization''s services, system components (infrastructure, software, people, procedures, data), control environment, and system boundaries. This section enables user entities to compare providers'' control environments and assess suitability.
Wrong (A): The engagement letter is an administrative document between the auditor and service organization, not intended for user entity evaluation or provider comparison.
Wrong (B): The management assertion confirms that management believes the description is accurate, but it does not contain the detailed operational information needed for comparison.
Wrong (C): The CUECs section lists controls the user entity must implement — it describes the user''s responsibilities, not the provider''s control environment.$EXPL$
