-- Q3916: SOC Testing Controls [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per AT-C Section 320.A38 (SSAE No. 18), inspection of badge access logs provides the strongest evidence because documentary evidence covering the entire examination period demonstrates all entries, including anomalies or unauthorized access attempts. Log review enables the auditor to identify patterns, exceptions, and trends across the full period.
Wrong (B): Inquiry of management alone lacks corroborative evidence and is the least persuasive form of audit evidence under professional standards.
Wrong (C): Observation of a single employee entry covers only one moment in time and does not provide evidence about control effectiveness throughout the period.
Wrong (D): Vendor marketing materials are not audit evidence — they describe product capabilities, not actual control operation at the specific data center.$EXPL$
