-- Q3917: SOC Testing Controls [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): For a high-risk weekly control with 52 occurrences and zero expected deviations, a sample of approximately 20 to 25 items is appropriate per the AICPA Audit Sampling Guide and AT-C Section 205 testing requirements. The larger sample reflects the high-risk assessment and low tolerable deviation rate, providing greater assurance of operating effectiveness.
Wrong (A): Testing only 5 occurrences provides insufficient coverage for a high-risk control and would not achieve the needed confidence level.
Wrong (C): Testing all 52 occurrences is unnecessary — statistical sampling provides sufficient assurance without examining every instance, balancing rigor with efficiency.
Wrong (D): Testing only the most recent occurrence provides no evidence about control operation during the rest of the examination period.$EXPL$
