Wrong (A): Minor issues that were promptly corrected would not warrant an adverse opinion — such findings might result in a qualified opinion or no modification at all.
Wrong (B): An adverse opinion is a definitive conclusion, not an indication that the report is incomplete or that additional testing is needed.
