UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 315.A128, the completeness assertion addresses whether all transactions and events that should have been recorded have in fact been recorded. Unposted December purchase transactions represent potential understatement — items that exist in reality but are missing from the financial statements.
Wrong (B): The existence assertion addresses the opposite direction — whether recorded assets, liabilities, and transactions actually exist or occurred, which relates to potential overstatement rather than omission.
Wrong (C): The valuation assertion addresses whether assets, liabilities, and equity interests are recorded at appropriate amounts, not whether all items have been captured.
Wrong (D): Rights and obligations addresses whether the entity holds or controls the rights to assets and has incurred the recorded obligations, not whether transactions were recorded.$EXPL$
