  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 315.A128, the existence assertion addresses whether assets recorded in the financial statements actually exist at a given date. Physically verifying that recorded inventory items are present in the warehouse directly tests existence through observation procedures per AU-C 501.03.
Wrong (A): The completeness assertion addresses the opposite direction — whether all items that should be recorded have been included, not whether recorded items physically exist.
