-- Q4913: Change Management [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 200.05, reasonable assurance is a high, but not absolute, level of assurance obtained when the auditor has gathered sufficient appropriate audit evidence to reduce audit risk to an acceptably low level. Inherent limitations of an audit — including sampling and the persuasive nature of evidence — prevent absolute assurance.
Wrong (B): A moderate level of assurance describes a review engagement under AR-C 90, which provides limited (not reasonable) assurance through inquiry and analytical procedures.
Wrong (C): Absolute assurance is not achievable due to inherent audit limitations — reasonable assurance explicitly acknowledges that some risk of undetected misstatement remains.
Wrong (D): A low level of assurance based on inquiry and analytical procedures describes a review engagement, not an audit, which requires detailed substantive testing.$EXPL$
