-- Q4924: Change Management [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Bypassing all approval, testing, and documentation requirements with no retrospective review represents the greatest control weakness per COBIT BAI06 and ITIL change management standards. Without any compensating control, there is no mechanism to ensure emergency changes are appropriate, effective, or recorded.
Wrong (A): Verbal approval from the IT director before implementation provides a compensating control — while not ideal, it ensures some authorization occurs before the change is made.
Wrong (B): Documenting within 24 hours and obtaining CAB review at the next meeting is an acceptable compensating control that balances urgency with retrospective governance.
Wrong (D): Limiting emergency changes to a predefined list of authorized personnel is a reasonable preventive control that reduces the risk of inappropriate changes.$EXPL$
