-- Q4946: SOC Report Content and Structure [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Per AT-C Section 320.31, the management description of the system in a SOC report covers the five components that make up the system boundary: infrastructure, software, people, procedures, and data. This description is prepared by management and provides context for the controls being examined.
Wrong (A): The auditor''s opinion on control effectiveness is presented in a separate section of the report — it is not part of management''s system description.
Wrong (C): The user entity''s internal control environment is the responsibility of the user entity, not the service organization, and is not included in the service organization''s system description.
Wrong (D): While subservice organizations may be mentioned in the system description, their financial statements are not included — only their role in service delivery is described.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4946;

-- Q4947: SOC Report Content and Structure [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): In a SOC 2 Type II report, per AT-C Section 205, management''s assertion addresses both the suitability of design and the operating effectiveness of controls throughout the specified examination period. A Type I report, by contrast, only addresses suitability of design as of a point in time.
Wrong (B): Management''s assertion does not claim compliance with all applicable laws and regulations — it is limited to the design and operating effectiveness of controls against the Trust Services Criteria.
Wrong (C): The assertion does not guarantee that no security breaches occurred — it addresses whether controls were designed and operated effectively, not the absence of incidents.
Wrong (D): Management''s assertion pertains to the service organization''s own controls, not to shifting responsibility for implementing all controls to user entities.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4947;

-- Q4949: SOC Report Content and Structure [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Per AT-C Section 320, complementary user entity controls (CUECs) are controls that the service organization''s system design assumes the user entity has in place. If user entities do not implement CUECs, the overall control objectives may not be achieved even if the service organization''s own controls operate effectively.
Wrong (B): The user entity cannot ignore CUECs — the service organization''s controls are designed with the assumption that CUECs are in place, making them necessary for complete control coverage.
Wrong (C): CUECs are not optional recommendations — they are essential components of the complete control environment required for control objectives to be met.
Wrong (D): CUECs are specifically designed to be implemented by the user entity within its own environment; requesting the service organization implement them misunderstands their purpose.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 4949;
